},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"1"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4587985","displayName":"Mark Kastelic","shortName":"M. Kastelic"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4565226","displayName":"Alex Turcotte","shortName":"A. Turcotte"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1824","guid":"58cac4d0-a208-3028-b2a6-ff7aba657bc3","fullName":"TD Garden","address":{"city":"Boston","state":"MA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1824.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17850,"officials":[{"fullName":"Justin Kea","displayName":"Justin Kea","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Furman South","displayName":"Furman South","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kyle Flemington","displayName":"Kyle Flemington","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Ryan Jackson","displayName":"Ryan Jackson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Darcy Kuemper stops 29 shots for 40th career shutout in Kings' 3-0 win over Bruins","description":"— Darcy Kuemper stopped 29 shots for his 40th career shutout, including Morgan Geekie’s third-period penalty shot, and Mats Zuccarello scored an early goal as the Los Angeles Kings beat the Boston Bruins 3-0 on Tuesday night to snap a four-game skid.","story":"BOSTON -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2610321/darcy-kuemper\">Darcy Kuemper</a> stopped 29 shots for his 40th career shutout, including Morgan Geekie’s third-period penalty shot, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5560/mats-zuccarello\">Mats Zuccarello</a> scored an early goal as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/la/los-angeles-kings\">Los Angeles Kings</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/bos/boston-bruins\">Boston Bruins</a> 3-0 on Tuesday night to snap a four-game skid.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4997131/andre-lee\">Andre Lee</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3891922/erik-gustafsson\">Erik Gustafsson</a> also scored for the Kings, who picked up just their sixth win.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4392765/michael-dipietro\">Michael DiPietro</a> made 19 saves for the Bruins, who lost their third straight for the first time this season.\n\n\r\n              Kuemper made a left-pad stop on Geekie’s penalty shot wrister en route to his first shutout this season.\n\n\r\n              The previous eight games in Boston between the teams were decided in overtime or a shootout, with the Kings winning five.\n\n\r\n              DiPietro made a splendid glove stop on Quinton Byfield’s second-period penalty shot. Byfield went wide left and cut in before firing a backhand shot.\n\n\r\n              Boston lost its last two games against two of the league’s better teams — <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/wild-bruins-score-0387e5a9324fb20a06910e0b1b96e8f0\">Minnesota</a> and <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/canadiens-bruins-score-92155745fe0d0e59c554d8b25f4907d4\">Montreal</a> — by a combined score of 11-4.\n\n\r\n              Coming into the game a point ahead of the West’s basement, the Kings went ahead 1-0 when Zuccarello’s wrister from the left circle slipped inside the near post 15:46 into the game.\n\n\r\n              Cutting in front, Lee had Scott Laughton’s pass carom in off his left knee in the second.\n\n\r\n              Los Angeles defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3995/drew-doughty\">Drew Doughty</a> played his 1,297th game with the club, moving past Dustin Brown for second on the team’s all-time list behind Anze Kopitar’s 1,521.\n\n\r\n              Boston <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/bruins-kings-score-69a6aac9ca0c1de13196acbe01a52e11\">won 4-1 in Los Angeles</a> on Oct. 17 in the teams’ other meeting this season.\n\n\r\n              The Kings came in with the NHL’s worst penalty kill percentage, allowing 11 goals in 22 chances, but kept Boston scoreless in two opportunities.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3891952/artemi-panarin\">Artemi Panarin</a>, who leads the Kings with 19 points in 17 games, missed his second straight game due to a family matter.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Kings: At Toronto on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Bruins: Travel to Detroit Wednesday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-18T15:11:58Z"}}